  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence is that RNA-only scvi_n200 with multiprofile is much better than image-only models, with config_005 and config_006 reaching about 0.65 validation accuracy and F1, while image-only models are only around 0.21-0.23. The key uncertainty is whether image features can complement the strong RNA representation at all. config_036 tests this directly by extending the strong scvi_n200 multiprofile avgpool RNA baseline with the slightly better single-image encoder, imagenet_vit_l, and a simple concat fusion. This keeps the RNA encoder, profile setting, and aggregation fixed, making it a clean first multimodal test: if it improves over the RNA-only baseline, it justifies further fusion and image-encoder experiments; if not, it argues against investing more budget in complex multimodal variants."
}

